 copd:{definition:'Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease: a long-term lung condition that damages the airways or lung tissue, restricts airflow, and makes breathing difficult; it commonly includes emphysema, chronic bronchitis, or both.',synonyms:['chronic obstructive pulmonary disease','chronic obstructive lung disease'],example:{word:'COPD',text:'Years of smoking can increase the risk of developing COPD.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'chronic obstructive pulmonary disease',text:'Years of smoking can increase the risk of developing chronic obstructive pulmonary disease.'},translation:{es:'epoc'}},
