 'total-loss':{definition:'An insurance classification for property, often a vehicle, that an insurer determines is uneconomical or not feasible to repair under the applicable policy and rules.',synonyms:['write-off (British usage)','constructive total loss (in some contexts)'],example:{word:'total loss',text:'The insurer declared the damaged car a total loss after assessing the repair costs.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'write-off',text:'The insurer treated the damaged car as a write-off after assessing the repair costs.'}},
