 premises:{definition:'A building, land, or other property occupied or used by a person or organization; in legal and formal use, the precise scope depends on context.',synonyms:['property','site','building and grounds (when referring to a location)'],example:{word:'premises',text:'Visitors must sign in before entering the premises.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'property',text:'Visitors must sign in before entering the property.'},translation:{es:'inmueble'}},
 conveyancer:{definition:'A legal professional who handles the legal work involved in transferring ownership of land or property, especially in England and Wales.',synonyms:['property transfer legal professional','licensed conveyancer (where regulated)'],example:{word:'conveyancer',text:'The conveyancer checked the contract and title documents before completion.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'property transfer legal professional',text:'The property transfer legal professional checked the contract and title documents before completion.'}},
 amortization:{definition:'The gradual repayment of a loan through scheduled payments over time; each payment may cover interest and reduce principal. In accounting, it can also mean allocating an intangible asset’s cost over time.',synonyms:['loan repayment schedule','amortisation (British spelling)'],example:{word:'amortization',text:'The loan’s amortization schedule shows how the balance falls with each payment.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'loan repayment schedule',text:'The loan repayment schedule shows how the balance falls with each payment.'},translation:{es:'amortizacion'}},
