  summons:{definition:'A formal legal notice requiring a person to appear before a court or respond to a legal proceeding. Its form, recipient, and required response depend on the procedure and jurisdiction.',synonyms:['notice to appear','court summons'],example:{word:'summons',text:'The court issued a summons requiring the company to respond to the claim.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'notice to appear',text:'The court issued a notice to appear requiring the company to respond to the claim.'}},
  'background-check':{definition:'A review of information about a person’s or organisation’s history for a particular purpose, such as assessing a job applicant or tenant. The records checked and rules governing their use vary by context and jurisdiction.',synonyms:['background screening','review of personal records'],example:{word:'background check',text:'The employer explained which records the background check would cover.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'background screening',text:'The employer explained which records the background screening would cover.'}},
  'cease-and-desist':{definition:'A demand or directive that someone stop a specified activity. A cease-and-desist letter may be sent by a private party and is not necessarily a court order; its legal effect depends on who issues it and the applicable law.',synonyms:['demand to stop an activity','cease-and-desist letter'],example:{word:'cease and desist',text:'The company received a cease-and-desist letter alleging trademark infringement.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'demand to stop an activity',text:'The company received a demand to stop an activity alleging trademark infringement.'}},
  'class-action':{definition:'A lawsuit in which one or more representatives bring claims on behalf of a larger group with common issues. A court must generally approve the group or class under the applicable rules; requirements differ by jurisdiction.',synonyms:['representative group lawsuit','class proceeding'],example:{word:'class action',text:'The court considered whether the consumers’ claims could proceed as a class action.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'class proceeding',text:'The court considered whether the consumers’ claims could proceed as a class proceeding.'}},
  'due-diligence':{definition:'Careful investigation and assessment of relevant facts, risks, and obligations before making a decision or entering a transaction. Its scope depends on the subject and the applicable legal or business context.',synonyms:['pre-transaction investigation','careful risk assessment'],example:{word:'due diligence',text:'The buyer completed due diligence before acquiring the business.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'pre-transaction investigation',text:'The buyer completed a pre-transaction investigation before acquiring the business.'}},
  'conflict-of-interest':{definition:'A situation in which a person’s personal, financial, or other interests could improperly influence, or appear to influence, their professional judgment or duty. It may be actual, potential, or perceived.',synonyms:['competing personal and professional interests','situation that may bias judgment'],example:{word:'conflict of interest',text:'She disclosed the conflict of interest before taking part in the decision.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'situation that may bias judgment',text:'She disclosed the situation that may bias judgment before taking part in the decision.'}},
  'jury-duty':{definition:'The obligation or period of service involved in being available for jury selection or serving as a juror, where the legal system provides for juries. Eligibility, exemptions, and procedures vary by jurisdiction.',synonyms:['jury service','service as a juror'],example:{word:'jury duty',text:'He checked the court website for instructions before reporting for jury duty.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'jury service',text:'He checked the court website for instructions before reporting for jury service.'}},
  'planning-permission':{definition:'In the UK, official approval required for certain development or changes to land or buildings under planning rules. Whether permission is needed depends on the proposal, location, and applicable rules.',synonyms:['planning consent','development permission'],example:{word:'planning permission',text:'They applied for planning permission before extending the house.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'planning consent',text:'They applied for planning consent before extending the house.'}},
  overqualified:{definition:'Having more education, experience, skills, or other qualifications than a particular role requires. The term describes a perceived mismatch and does not by itself explain a hiring decision.',synonyms:['more qualified than the role requires','having excess qualifications for a position'],example:{word:'overqualified',text:'Although she was overqualified for the entry-level role, she applied because she wanted to change careers.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'more qualified than the role requires',text:'Although she was more qualified than the role required, she applied because she wanted to change careers.'}}
