  'booster-dose':{definition:'An additional vaccine dose given after an initial dose or series to strengthen or restore protection when recommended. Timing and eligibility depend on the vaccine, person, and public-health guidance.',synonyms:['booster shot','additional vaccine dose'],example:{word:'booster dose',text:'Her clinician recommended a booster dose based on the current vaccination guidance.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'additional vaccine dose',text:'Her clinician recommended an additional vaccine dose based on the current vaccination guidance.'}},
  anesthesiologist:{definition:'A physician specialising in anaesthesia and perioperative care, including assessing patients, providing anaesthesia, and monitoring vital functions during procedures. Anaesthesia may make a patient unconscious or numb a particular area, depending on the type used.',synonyms:['anaesthesiologist','anesthesia specialist'],example:{word:'anesthesiologist',text:'The anesthesiologist discussed the options and risks of anesthesia with the patient before surgery.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'anesthesia specialist',text:'The anesthesia specialist discussed the options and risks of anesthesia with the patient before surgery.'}},
  'pay-off-a-mortgage':{word:'Pay off a mortgage',definition:'To repay the full amount owed under a mortgage loan. Paying it off may allow the lender’s security interest to be discharged or released, but that step can require separate paperwork under local rules.',synonyms:['repay a mortgage in full','settle a mortgage loan'],example:{word:'pay off a mortgage',text:'They saved for years to pay off their mortgage before retirement.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'repay a mortgage in full',text:'They saved for years to repay their mortgage in full before retirement.'}},
