  'age-group':{definition:'A category of people within a specified range of ages, used for comparison, eligibility, research, or planning. The range depends on the purpose.',synonyms:['age bracket','age band','group within an age range'],example:{word:'age group',text:'The survey compared health outcomes across each age group.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'age bracket',text:'The survey compared health outcomes across each age bracket.'}},
  torsion:{definition:'The act or state of twisting around an axis. In medicine, torsion can describe an organ or structure twisting in a way that may restrict its blood supply; the affected structure and consequences depend on the condition.',synonyms:['twisting','rotational twist','torsion injury (in some contexts)'],example:{word:'torsion',text:'The scan showed torsion of the ovary, a twisting that can affect its blood supply.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'twisting',text:'The scan showed twisting of the ovary, which can affect its blood supply.'}},
  'psychological-drive':{definition:'An internal motive or impulse that helps shape a person’s behaviour. The phrase may be used in general or in psychological theories, and does not necessarily imply that the motive is unconscious or uncontrollable.',synonyms:['internal motive','psychological motivation','inner impulse'],example:{word:'psychological drive',text:'The researcher examined how the need for belonging acted as a psychological drive.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'internal motive',text:'The researcher examined how the need for belonging acted as an internal motive.'}},
  oratory:{definition:'The art or practice of formal public speaking, especially speech intended to persuade or move an audience. In some contexts, an oratory is also a small chapel or place of prayer.',synonyms:['public speaking','the art of persuasive speech','small chapel (alternate sense)'],example:{word:'oratory',text:'Her oratory persuaded the audience, and the historic oratory next door served as a chapel.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'public speaking',text:'Her public speaking persuaded the audience, and the historic oratory next door served as a chapel.'}},
  'letter-rogatory':{definition:'A formal request from a court in one country to a court in another for judicial assistance, commonly to obtain testimony or other evidence from someone abroad. The procedure and scope depend on applicable treaties and local law.',synonyms:['letter of request for judicial assistance','international judicial request','letter of request (in some systems)'],example:{word:'letter rogatory',text:'The court issued a letter rogatory to seek testimony from a witness located abroad.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'letter of request for judicial assistance',text:'The court issued a letter of request for judicial assistance to seek testimony from a witness abroad.'}},
  licensure:{definition:'The process or status of receiving official permission from a government or regulatory authority to practise a profession or carry out a regulated activity. Requirements differ from certification and vary by jurisdiction.',synonyms:['professional licensing','granting of a licence','authorisation to practise'],example:{word:'licensure',text:'The board reviewed her qualifications as part of the professional licensure process.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'professional licensing',text:'The board reviewed her qualifications as part of the professional licensing process.'}},
  'family-reunification':{definition:'A process through which eligible family members separated by migration may join or live with a relative in another country under that country’s immigration rules. Eligibility, qualifying relationships, and procedures vary; it is not an unconditional right in every case.',synonyms:['family reunification process','family reunion through migration','family-reunification route'],example:{word:'family reunification',text:'The family applied for reunification and submitted the documents required by the immigration rules.'},exampleSynonym:{word:'family reunification process',text:'The family applied through the family reunification process and submitted the required documents.'}}
